- Volume of \ce{HCl} used for titration: \pu{18.50 cm^3}
- Concentration of \ce{HCl} solution: \pu{0.100 mol dm^{-3}}

First, calculate the moles of \ce{NaOH} added:
\[
\text{Moles of } \ce{NaOH} = \text{Volume} \times \text{Concentration} = \pu{40.00 cm^3} \times \pu{0.100 mol dm^{-3}} = \pu{0.00400 mol}
\]

Next, calculate the moles of \ce{HCl} used in the titration:
\[
\text{Moles of } \ce{HCl} = \text{Volume} \times \text{Concentration} = \pu{18.50 cm^3} \times \pu{0.100 mol dm^{-3}} = \pu{0.00185 mol}
\]

